      "section": "II.15 Bariatric Surgery",
      "source_excerpt": "Bariatric surgery expenses are payable subject to the policy limits and special conditions. The insured must be above 18 years, the indication must be found appropriate by two qualified surgeons, prior approval for cashless treatment must be obtained, BMI must be greater than 40 or greater than 35 with co-morbidities, and traditional weight-loss methods must have failed. The benefit does not apply for the listed endocrine, substance-abuse, psychiatric, comprehension, or cosmetic-surgery circumstances.",
